Progress (CopperWren). This is not independent verification: I implemented several P2 boundaries (3.7, 3.11–3.13, 3.15). NOT CLOSED: main is red from an sr-fzia regression; see the blocker below.
Delivered, in e27053f (pushed on eda9211):
(1) scripts/e2e/product/roster.json maps all 25 P2 e2e cases from the contract matrix to the real tests that establish them. scripts/e2e/product_cases.py checks the map statically: every mapped test is a #[test] fn in exactly one suite target, and every matrix case with its assertion IDs is covered. It evaluates each case from the actual cargo log: a case passes only if every mapped test appears exactly once as ok, and the run is complete (one ok summary per target, nothing failed, ignored or filtered, at least one passed). roster.sh now also runs quill_query, cli_config and p2_gate, and passes only if all cases pass.
(2) Ten stale P2 matrix unit references now name real tests. All P2 references resolve, and validate_contract_matrix passes with 79 declarations.
(3) tests/roster_import.rs importing_a_roster_mutates_nothing gives real evidence for the previously unbacked case dry-run-import-clean.
(4) Retained fixture trees now use timestamped, exclusive names. PID reuse had reused a stale tree.
The gate tests (tests/p2_gate.rs) landed inside eda9211, where MistyCoyote extended them for sr-fzia.
Evidence before sr-fzia, at 61188e0 plus my files including my fail-closed p2_gate:
- roster product suite: 25/25 cases, 135 tests across 16 targets, 0 failed/ignored/filtered (RCH vmi1152480);
- full suite: 57 binaries, 517 passed, 0 failed, 3 ignored;
- clippy --all-targets -D warnings clean;
- check_dependency_graph.py passed: 4 feature sets, normal/build/dev edges, all targets, no tantivy or other banned packages;
- test_product_cases.py 8/8;
- a planted missing test marks its case missing and the suite failed (24/25) on the real log.
Blocker: at eda9211 plus my files, the full suite has 1 failure: roster_failures changed_membership_and_hostile_metadata_never_become_publishable. That test asserts the global withholding which sr-fzia intentionally scoped. I reopened sr-fzia for its owner to update the contract deliberately. 3.17 closes after the roster suite is green on main.
Review findings recorded: 4.14 was reopened because its e2e evidence was the runner-mechanics fixture, not product tests. sr-fzia was filed for global authority withholding.

description:
Observed on the maintainer machine's real Claude transcripts. In 32 of about 190, the latest record the native parser maps to a user message is not a prompt the user gave:
- 22 isMeta injected content (skill bodies, scheduled prompts, caveats);
- 7 <local-command-stdout> output;
- 2 '[Request interrupted by user]' markers;
- 1 compaction summary (isCompactSummary).
Newer records also mark origin: promptSource 'system' vs 'typed'/'queued'/'sdk'/'suggestion_accepted', and origin.kind 'task-notification'/'auto-continuation'/'peer' vs 'human'.
rank --transcript and bare discovery take the latest user message as the current request, so these sessions rank the wrong request.
Scope: the native Claude parser classifies such records as system context. They stay in bounded history but are never the current request. These are unverified harness conventions: unflagged older records keep today's behavior.
